WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
You know, there are few things Riot Games loves more than a good storyline.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.200
And there are few storylines better than that of the underdog.

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:13.540
You know, David vs Goliath, the Misfits vs SKT if you will.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:19.720
That's why this week we decided to give you the top 10 underdog moments in League of Legends.

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:27.740
These are the one-off upset victories, or the Cinderella bracket runs that made us want to stand up and cheer for the little guy.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:35.560
These are the underdog wins or near wins that warmed our cold shriveled esports hearts.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:40.580
So without further ado guys, let's get into it with the top 10 underdog moments in League

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:46.760
Before 2014 no one gave an international wild-card team a second look.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:54.280
The 10th spot on our list belongs to a team that blew up Group D at the 2014 world championship. KaBuM!.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:02.880
The first seed from Europe, Alliance were locked in a dead heat with the second NA seed in Cloud 9 and the favored Koreans

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:04.560
NaJin White Shield.

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:11.200
Their match against KaBuM! was more important than ever. A win would put C9 into a must win-situation

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.260
against NaJin to force a three way tie-breaker.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:19.880
What was expected to be Alliance brushing aside the wildcard turned into KaBuM!

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:24.060
surprising everyone with their early aggression and forcing Alliance into

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.720
uncharacteristically bad team fights.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:48.640
(Casting)

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:55.600
Alliance was pushed all the way back to their base, but KaBuM! never let up and overthrew the Kings of Europe.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:02:16.080
(Casting)

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:19.760
C9 will go on to beat Najin to eliminate Europe's best

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:27.160
hope for a world championship in forming a bond with the Brazilian wildcard that had proven the world wrong.

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:30.960
"Since Kabum beat Alliance, that win was for them."

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:34.560
"This is for KaBuM!"

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:41.320
With one of the biggest upset runs in NA LCS playoff history, our number nine moment comes from Good Game

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:45.060
University in the inaugural NA LCS Playoffs.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:52.420
During the regular season GGU you played their role of a middling team well with an 11-17 record,

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:58.280
going negative against each of the top three teams, and barely avoiding the promotion tournament.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:04.660
No one gave this team of fresh faces much of a chance against the third seeded Dignitas.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:11.560
(Casting)

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.500
Then moved on to face the number two seeded Curse.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:22.000
(Casting)

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:29.500
Once again GGU won the series 2-1 and found themselves in the finals against the number one seeded TSM.

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:34.200
"TSM comes in to this match at the top seed in playoffs, and the hottest team in the LCS"

00:03:34.620 --> 00:03:38.360
TSM, to no one’s surprise, took a clean game one.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:45.980
But, GGU exploded out of the gate in game two winning a perfect 27 minute game.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:04:05.920
(Casting)

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:14.640
After two more back-and-forth games GGU managed to do what no one could have expected and took TSM to a decisive game 5.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:18.480
Although they didn’t manage to overcome the kings of NA in the end,

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:24.940
GGU proved that your regular season record doesn’t matter and that in the playoffs, anything is possible.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:30.240
"From 12 and 2 to the championship game, taking 2nd place in the Spring Split."

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.540
Quite a run, they took TSM to all five games."

00:04:33.980 --> 00:04:37.060
Forced to play their way into Worlds 2017,

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:40.240
the number eight moment on our list goes to Fnatic.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:45.920
The third European seed found themselves in a group with with the top North American and Korean seeds

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:50.460
as well as one of the strongest wildcard teams to ever attend Worlds.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:59.080
Unfortunately for the Europeans, the first four days seemed to play out as expected with Fnatic losing their first four games of the tournament.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:02.320
To even have a chance at making it out of groups,

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.320
they needed to win their next two games and hope for a tie-breaker scenario.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:14.200
"Nobody has ever qualified for quarterfinals after starting the tournament 0-3 in week one."

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:19.560
Fnatic did their part with their deliberate team fighting to force a three-way tiebreaker.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:26.480
(Casting)

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:30.760
"And Fnatic they needed to win and they have done it."

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:36.920
The team would play Immortals with the winner taking on the Gigabyte Marines for the final spot in the Quarterfinals.

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:40.260
Their teamwork proved too much for Immortals.

00:05:40.260 --> 00:06:00.380
(Casting)

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:05.840
Fnatic was one win away from becoming the first team to make the Quarterfinals after going down

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:09.110
0-4. In a bloody back-and-forth game

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:15.060
Fnatic's superior macro play earned them the win and a trip to the Worlds Quarterfinals.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:30.360
(Casting)

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.400
Although they’d soon fall 3-1 to Royal Never Give Up,

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:41.660
it was their miraculous escape from the near death sentence that is an 0-4 record that earns them a spot on this list.

00:06:41.660 --> 00:06:45.880
"So many expectations defied by Fnatic."

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:53.500
"No one in this group stage format has come back from an 0-3 let alone in 0-4."

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:59.580
"An absolutely miraculous run, a Cinderella story for Fnatic."

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:08.160
From Challenger, all the way to Worlds. The seventh spot on our list belongs to the famous run from Origen in 2015.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:15.280
The team rolled their way through EU Challenger only dropping a single game and qualified for the EU LCS Summer Split.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:18.440
Origen proved they had what it took to play in the LCS,

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:26.140
crushing their way through the split never falling lower than third, winning EU’s third spot at Worlds through the regional qualifier.

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:38.380
(Casting)

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:42.260
In a group with KT Rolster, LGD and TSM,

00:07:42.260 --> 00:07:49.660
no one expected Origen to even make it out of groups. But once again Origen rose to the challenge,

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:54.400
advancing out of the group to the Quarterfinals against the LMS’ Flash Wolves.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:58.340
"I have experience playing against them in a best of five and they are very energetic throughout."

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:02.640
"They are good at adapting, their coach understands the draft and how to adapt properly."

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:05.720
"So I expect them to do exactly the same in this matches."

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:13.180
Origen proved they weren’t just masters of the best-of-one and took the series 3-1 to move on to the Semifinals.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:24.920
(Casting)

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:29.060
While their run was stopped, as many are, at the hands of SKT,

00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:35.060
Origen proved that a team with the right chemistry can climb to just about any height.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:51.560
Our number six entry on this list comes from the 2016 Mid Season Invitational.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:09:01.040
Off the back of their first 2nd consecutive domestic championship, Counter Logic Gaming faced down four daunting opponents.

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:07.720
After going 2-2 in the first two days CLG got a chance at a breakthrough against SKT.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:14.020
After being down for more than 40 minutes CLG managed to hold on and find an opening.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:27.600
(Casting)

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:33.940
After SKT took their revenge on Day four, CLG matched up against the undefeated Royal Never Give Up.

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:43.300
The early game swung in RNG’s favor but, CLG held on again and at 37 minutes Xmithie turned the entire game on it’s head.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:10:22.280
(Casting)

00:10:22.340 --> 00:10:29.520
After taking out Flash Wolves in the Semifinals, CLG could not overcome Faker and SKT in the finals.

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:35.800
But, with this run they had proven that NA was a serious contender on the international stage.

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:41.100
(Casting)

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:47.680
Let’s be honest here, nearly everyone is an underdog when facing down SKT.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:52.380
Rounding out the top five is the little EU team that could in Misfits.

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:56.280
Coming all the way from Challenger the previous season,

00:10:56.280 --> 00:11:02.340
Misfits finished second in the Summer Split to secure the second EU seed at Worlds.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:08.760
They managed to squeak out of groups with a 3-3 record after winning a tiebreaker against TSM.

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:18.720
(Casting)

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:25.720
Now the European darkhorse had their toughest test, the Korean dynasty SK Telecom T1.

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:31.140
"I mean it's very exciting. It would also be a massive upset of anything other than the expected result happens."

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:34.680
"I mean, it's SK Telecom T1 we're used to seeing this team in the final."

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:41.460
After losing the first game Misfits held strong, winning an impeccable game two on the back of their team coordination.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:12:09.740
(Casting)

00:12:09.900 --> 00:12:15.500
In game three, all bets were off with IgNar’s Ferver Leona pick in the bot lane.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:19.600
(Casting)

00:12:19.600 --> 00:12:23.920
Misfits had a plan and managed to secure the first two kills of the game.

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:46.760
(Casting)

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:51.480
They managed to hold on to their lead to take a 2-1 series lead.

00:12:51.480 --> 00:13:02.440
(Casting)

00:13:02.680 --> 00:13:08.320
Eventually, experience won the day and SKT managed to stave off the Misfits onslaught

00:13:08.320 --> 00:13:12.000
and capitalize on mistakes to win game four and five.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:16.600
"So much credit over to Misfits, like what a performance in this series."

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.620
"So few people thought they could do anything against SKT."

00:13:19.620 --> 00:13:26.780
"Game 1 was a complete stomp. 25 minutes in favor of SKT, and then they bounce back for these off meta picks."

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:32.500
"We get Leona, we get Blitzcrank, they win two games in a row. Even in the slow games here game four and five;

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:40.320
they were so close to actually beating SKT. It was definitely not a late game just purely in favor of the Korean team."

00:13:41.080 --> 00:13:44.780
Misfits shocked the world in 2017,

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:50.800
they were one teamfight away from the biggest upset League had ever seen.

00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:53.760
"From Challenger to almost champion killers."

00:13:54.260 --> 00:14:01.140
When you think of underdogs in League of Legends you probably think of the International Wildcard spot at Worlds.

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:07.480
In the fourth spot on our list goes to the most historic wildcard run in league history.

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:11.860
"This is insane they are actually beating the ROX Tigers right now."

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:18.400
Albus Nox Luna came in to Worlds 2016 with precisely zero expectations.

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:21.960
They weren’t even considered the best Wildcard team at the tournament.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:29.480
After a bloody but decisive loss to the ROX Tigers everyone's expectations seemed to be coming true.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:32.160
But Albus Nox had other plans.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:34.300
They beat CLG,

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:37.360
G2, and then CLG again.

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:43.640
One more win and they would be the first Wildcard to make it out of groups.

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:52.320
(Casting)

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:54.960
And Albus Nox did not disappoint.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:15:00.560
In an almost 70 minute bloodbath they kept the tournament favorites against the ropes

00:15:00.560 --> 00:15:06.500
and managed to become the most successful Wildcard team in League of legends history.

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:43.620
(Casting)

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:51.180
"Hey guys, we are from Wildcard. And as I have told you before; being underdog doesn't mean being a loser. That's all."

00:15:56.900 --> 00:16:07.860
In our bronze medal moment from IEM Katowice 2015, the LPL’s most unlikely hero challenged Korea’s dominance on the international stage.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:17.020
The GE Tigers were having an incredible split with a perfect 10 and 0 record and had a combined game score of 20 and 2.

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:24.080
World Elite only had a single series win to their name and a game score of 8 and 22.

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:31.780
But by edging out OMG and EDG at the IEM Shenzhen qualifier, WE won a spot in Katowice.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:35.870
"That's the really scary thing about World Elite is that the language barrier, the roster changes,

00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:40.849
they're still trying to find their synergy. And the fact that they're dismantling top tier teams in the LPL with uhh,

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:44.599
kind of a lack of synergy, kind of speaks to the strength of the players right now."

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.180
"Can you imagine when they were finally firing on all cylinders."

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:53.720
The Tigers blew through their group, knocking down Cloud9 and SK Gaming to qualify for the Semifinals.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:17:03.040
World Elite took a tougher road. After losing to TSM they went on to knock out Gambit and the second Korean seed in CJ Entus.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.760
And so the stage was set in the Semifinal.

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:12.680
The Tigers won game one as expected, but in game two World Elite held on,

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:18.800
and after winning a scrappy dragon fight, they took over forcing a decisive game three.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:44.660
(Casting)

00:17:44.820 --> 00:17:51.420
"I mean we could see WE take this game, It's now down to that best of one. And I mean going into this match

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:55.480
it can't be understated, if the the GE Tigers lose this game

00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:59.860
This is undoubtedly the biggest upset in League of Legends history."

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:06.480
After grabbing an early lead, World Elite never looked back and completely destroyed the Tigers

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:12.040
in what could only be described at the time as the greatest upset League had ever seen.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:19:02.740
(Casting)

00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:08.000
On the back of big shakeups to North America’s longest standing roster,

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:14.220
our runner-up moment comes from Cloud9 at the 2015 NA Regional Qualifier.

00:19:14.220 --> 00:19:23.500
Ya see, C9 barely avoided relegation during the 2015 summer split and had one last shot at worlds.

00:19:23.500 --> 00:19:24.220
The Gauntlet.

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:27.720
"As strange as it sounds to call Cloud9 a Cinderella story,

00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:31.860
they could go on a miracle run to secure their third consecutive appearance at Worlds

00:19:31.860 --> 00:19:33.880
They reverse swept Gravity.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:45.400
(Casting)

00:19:45.480 --> 00:19:48.000
They reverse swept Team Impulse.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:57.440
(Casting)

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:06.180
C9 came together when it mattered most and managed to topple Team Liquid earning their third consecutive spot at Worlds.

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:27.800
(Casting)

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:32.780
Taking the top spot on our list is a run so storied, so impressive,

00:20:32.780 --> 00:20:40.200
it’s become one of the most iconic underdog stories in all of esports, not just League of Legends.

00:20:40.740 --> 00:20:46.800
Taipei Assassins entered the 2012 World Championship as a complete dark horse

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:51.460
and were staring down three of the best teams in the entire tournament.

00:20:51.740 --> 00:21:00.180
They took out a surging NaJin Sword in a 2-0 sweep and bounced back after a tough game one to defeat one of the tournament favorites,

00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:04.240
Moscow 5, to earn themselves a spot in the finals.

00:21:04.260 --> 00:21:29.420
(Casting)

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:35.840
But, it was there where they faced their final boss, the Korean juggernauts Azubu Frost.

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:42.980
Now, you have to understand here, Azubu Frost had decimated the competition up to this point,

00:21:43.060 --> 00:21:46.400
mangling the best teams in the world to get to this final,

00:21:46.580 --> 00:21:52.960
and no one thought a relatively unknown team from Taiwan would be the ones to challenge them.

00:21:52.960 --> 00:21:58.060
"Azubu Frost, they lost out on the five regional winners drawnings, and they were the ones that got stuck in the group stage."

00:21:58.060 --> 00:22:01.580
"And they proved that they're one of the best. Crushed the group stage,

00:22:01.780 --> 00:22:06.060
beat up on SoloMid and then they had that close three-game set in the Semifinals."

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:09.240
"If I had to guess the crowd favorite here is going to be the Taipei Assassins."

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:15.620
"It's an underdog story, people put power rankings out before this tournament. Who do you think has a chance? They were ranked 10th there, they were ranked 6th."

00:22:16.180 --> 00:22:19.140
"They've proven to the world that they deserve to be there."

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:26.480
After losing a close game one, TPA proceeded to dismantle the Korean champions in three back-to-back games.

00:22:26.480 --> 00:23:49.900
(Casting)

00:23:49.900 --> 00:23:53.420
The Taipei Assassins overcame incredible odds

00:23:53.420 --> 00:24:00.720
and three potential tournament winners to become League of Legends' greatest underdog story.

00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:21.700
Well guys, that's our list.

00:24:21.700 --> 00:24:27.600
Now, if you are still watching, I have one question for you. Why? The video is over go to the comments section?

00:24:27.600 --> 00:24:30.380
Maybe go watch a story of. I don't know live your life.

